---
description: |
  Normalizes Linux Audit `audit.log` lines to OCSF.

  ```tql
  from_file "/var/log/audit/audit.log" {
    read_lines
  }
  auditd::ocsf::normalize
  ```

  The operator parses each line, assembles the records of one audit event,
  combines the audit events of one login, maps the result to OCSF, and keeps
  the original lines in `raw_data`. It reads
  the native `RAW` and `ENRICHED` log formats, with or without the `node=`
  prefix that the audit daemon adds for `name_format` and that forwarded
  events carry.

  Use `auditd::parse`, `auditd::assemble`, `auditd::aggregate`, and
  `auditd::ocsf::map` instead for a staged pipeline, or to map each record on
  its own.
args:
  positional:
    - name: line
      description: The field holding the `audit.log` line.
      type: field
      default: line
  named:
    - name: into
      description: The field that receives the OCSF event.
      type: field
      default: this
---

$into._line = $line
auditd::parse $into._line, $into._audit
auditd::assemble $into._line, $into._audit
auditd::aggregate $into._audit
auditd::ocsf::map $into._audit, $into._ocsf
$into = $into._ocsf
